{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.ClosedFormInterfaceFactors","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedFormInterfaceFactors","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":48,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.trace_interface_bond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.trace_interface_bond","kind":"theorem","line":591,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L591-L601","doc":"**Trace bridge**: when the Markov trace's `z_param` is the closed form's\n`markovZ s`, the trace of the bridge crossing `σ_i + d_k·1` is exactly the\ninterface factor `f_k(q)` — connecting the Phase-5q factors to the\n`QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace` class (single-bond case; the two-bond case follows\nfrom `trace_bond_pair_factorizes`, and the general `A`-bond factorization\nawaits the cross-level Markov axiom, per the module docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.interfaceFactor_eq_bond_expectation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.interfaceFactor_eq_bond_expectation","kind":"theorem","line":576,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L576-L582","doc":"Each interface factor is the conditional expectation `z + d_k` of its\nbridge crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.bondD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.bondD","kind":"def","line":568,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L568-L574","doc":"Constant coefficient `d_k` of the bridge crossing `σ + d_k·1` realising\ninterface kind `k` (p-p: `0`; n-n: `−h`; p-n: `−h·(1/2 − δ/4)`) — the\n`(c, d)` data of `MarkovBondFactor.lean` with `c = 1` throughout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.closedFormTauM_deuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.closedFormTauM_deuteron","kind":"theorem","line":558,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L558-L564","doc":"**Deuteron instance** (`Z = N = 1`, the `H₆` anchor of the exact-ℚ\nverification): `tr_M(𝓑_D) = τ_p · τ_n · f_pn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.closedFormTauM_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.closedFormTauM_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":542,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L542-L556","doc":"**Canonical closed form** for an atom with `Z ≥ 1` protons and `N ≥ 1`\nneutrons:\n\n  `tr_M(𝓑_K) = τ_p^Z · τ_n^N · f_pp^{Z−1} · f_nn^{N−1} · f_pn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.canonicalInterfaceKinds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.canonicalInterfaceKinds","kind":"def","line":532,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L532-L540","doc":"Canonical interface list of the `p^Z n^N` ordering\n(`closed_form_tau_M.canonical_interface_kinds`, bring_color_weighted\nlabels): `Z−1` p-p bonds, then one p-n bond (when both species are\npresent), then `N−1` n-n bonds. Nat subtraction handles the `Z = 0` /\n`N = 0` edge cases exactly as the Python (`A < 2 → []`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.closedFormProduct_eq_pow_counts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.closedFormProduct_eq_pow_counts","kind":"theorem","line":515,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L515-L530","doc":"The interface product depends only on the interface **census**:\n`∏_i f_i = f_pp^{#pp} · f_nn^{#nn} · f_pn^{#pn}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.closedFormTauM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.closedFormTauM","kind":"def","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L508-L513","doc":"**Assembly layer of the Phase-5q closed form**: the full closed-form\nvalue `tr_M³(𝓑_p)^Z · tr_M³(𝓑_n)^N · ∏_i f_i(q)` from the two `H₃`\nbuilding blocks (`closed_form_tau_M.closed_form_tau_M`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.closedFormProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.closedFormProduct","kind":"def","line":504,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L504-L506","doc":"The interface product `∏_i f_i(q)` over an interface list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.interfaceFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.interfaceFactor","kind":"def","line":498,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L498-L502","doc":"Per-interface factor `f_i(q)` of the closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.instReprInterfaceKind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.instReprInterfaceKind","kind":"instance","line":496,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L496-L496","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.instReprInterfaceKind.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.instReprInterfaceKind.repr","kind":"def","line":496,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L496-L496","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.instDecidableEqInterfaceKind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.instDecidableEqInterfaceKind","kind":"instance","line":496,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L496-L496","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.InterfaceKind.pn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.InterfaceKind.pn","kind":"ctor","line":495,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L495-L495","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.InterfaceKind.nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.InterfaceKind.nn","kind":"ctor","line":494,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L494-L494","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.InterfaceKind.pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.InterfaceKind.pp","kind":"ctor","line":493,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L493-L493","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.InterfaceKind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.InterfaceKind","kind":"inductive","line":489,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L489-L496","doc":"The three interface kinds of the canonical atomic braid `𝓑_K`\n(`closed_form_tau_M.canonical_interface_kinds`): p-p (positive crossing),\nn-n (negative crossing), p-n (bring-color-weighted averaged crossing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPN_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPN_one","kind":"theorem","line":480,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L480-L485","doc":"Confluence at `q = 1`: the p-n factor collapses onto the p-p factor\n(`h(1) = 0` kills both the averaging and the flavor terms). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fNN_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fNN_one","kind":"theorem","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L473-L478","doc":"Confluence at `q = 1`: the n-n factor collapses onto the p-p factor\n(`h(1) = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPN_four_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPN_four_mul","kind":"theorem","line":459,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L459-L471","doc":"Division-free bridging form `4·f_pn = 4z − (2 − δ)·h` — the shape used\nby the Markov-step identity `τ_M(α·(4σ − (2−δ)h·1)) = (4z − (2−δ)h)·τ_M(α)`\n(cf. `QOU.BraidKnot.interface_knot_markov_z_bar_symmetric` for the δ = 0\ncase). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPN_eq_skein_avg_add_flavor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPN_eq_skein_avg_add_flavor","kind":"theorem","line":441,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L441-L457","doc":"**The bring-color-weighted p-n factor is the skein-symmetric chirality\naverage plus the flavor-split correction**:\n\n  `f_pn = (f_pp + f_nn)/2 + h·δ/4`.\n\nAt `δ = 0` this recovers the strict-averaged convention `z − h/2`; the\n`h·δ/4` term is the quaternionic color-tube asymmetry\n(`closed_form_tau_M` §\"bring_color_weighted\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPP_add_fNN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPP_add_fNN","kind":"theorem","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L427-L439","doc":"`f_pp + f_nn = 2z − h`: twice the strict-averaged interface factor\n`z − h/2`, the combination symmetric under the **skein** bar `σ ↦ σ⁻¹`\n(`interface_knot_markov_z_bar_symmetric`).\n\nUnder convention D it is **also** invariant under the `q`-bar of §3, because\nthe bar exchanges the two summands exactly (`fPP_bar_eq_fNN`,\n`fNN_bar_eq_fPP`) rather than merely rescaling them — see\n`strictAvg_bar_invariant`. Under convention C it was not: there `q`-bar fixes\n`z` while flipping `h`, so `z − h/2 ↦ z + h/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPP_mul_fNN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPP_mul_fNN","kind":"theorem","line":420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L420-L425","doc":"`f_pp · f_nn = z² − z·h`: the p-p/n-n product needed by the closed\nform's Laurent-degree bookkeeping (probe 9b). Pure ring identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.heckeH_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.heckeH_one","kind":"theorem","line":414,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L414-L416","doc":"`h(1) = 0`: the skein parameter vanishes at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.flavorDelta_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.flavorDelta_one","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L410-L412","doc":"`δ(1) = 0`: no flavor split at the classical point `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.flavorDelta_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.flavorDelta_factored","kind":"theorem","line":396,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L396-L408","doc":"**Exact cubic-vanishing factorization** (the leading-order identity):\n\n  `δ(q) = (q−1)³ · (q³+q²+q+1) / (3q⁴)`,\n\nexhibiting the third-order zero of the flavor split at `q = 1` exactly —\nthe algebraic content of the `δ ≈ (4/3)(q−1)³` leading order. Stated in\n`s` with `q = s²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.flavorDelta_eq_hbar_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.flavorDelta_eq_hbar_form","kind":"theorem","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L387-L394","doc":"**Structural identity** `δ = ℏ_q² · h · [2]_q / 3`\n(prop:flavor-split-substrate; `_li_2_q_util.flavor_split_leading`\ndocstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.strictAvg_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.strictAvg_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L365-L383","doc":"**The strict-averaged interface factor is `q`-bar INVARIANT under\nconvention D**: `z(q⁻¹) − h(q⁻¹)/2 = z(q) − h(q)/2`.\n\nBeing a symmetriser (`strictAvg_eq_bar_symmetriser`) it could hardly be\notherwise. The `2 ≠ 0` hypothesis is not boilerplate: in characteristic 2 the\naverage is not defined and the statement degenerates, exactly as in\n`QOU.MassTheory.PnInterfaceBarStructure`, which assumes `CharZero` for the\nsame reason. Stated separately because it is the claim that the header of this\nfile briefly denied: the bar flips the sign of `h`, and *that flip is exactly\nwhat cancels the shift* `z ↦ z − h`.\n\nConvention C behaves oppositely — there `z` is bar-fixed, so the flipped `h`\nhas nothing to cancel against and the defect is `h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.strictAvg_eq_bar_symmetriser","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.strictAvg_eq_bar_symmetriser","kind":"theorem","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L354-L363","doc":"**The strict-averaged interface factor is the `q`-bar symmetriser**:\n`z − h/2 = (z(q) + z(q⁻¹))/2`.\n\n`s`-variable twin of `QOU.MassTheory.strictPn_eq_barSymmetriser`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fNN_bar_eq_fPP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fNN_bar_eq_fPP","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L344-L352","doc":"**…and back**: `f_nn(q⁻¹) = f_pp(q)`. Together with `fPP_bar_eq_fNN` this\nsays the two like-flavour factors are a single two-element orbit of the\ninvolution — the sharp form of `fNN_bar_weight`, whose right-hand side\n`z/q⁴ + h` is `f_pp` written the long way round. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPP_bar_eq_fNN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPP_bar_eq_fNN","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L337-L342","doc":"**The bar carries the p-p factor onto the n-n factor exactly**, with no\nresidual weight: `f_pp(q⁻¹) = f_nn(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.markovZ_bar_eq_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.markovZ_bar_eq_shift","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L329-L335","doc":"**The `q`-bar of `z` is the shift by `−h`**: `z(q⁻¹) = z(q) − h(q)`.\n\nThe `s`-variable twin of `QOU.MassTheory.barZ`; obtained by composing\n`markovZ_bar_weight` with `markovZ_weight_eq_shift`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.markovZ_weight_eq_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.markovZ_weight_eq_shift","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L311-L327","doc":"**The weight-`−4` scaling and the `−h` shift are the same map.**\n\n`z/q⁴ = z − h` is an identity of convention D, not a coincidence at one point:\n\n  `z/q⁴ = q³/(q⁴(q²+1)) = 1/(q(q²+1))`,\n  `z − h = q³/(q²+1) − (q²−1)/q = (q⁴ − (q⁴−1))/(q(q²+1)) = 1/(q(q²+1))`.\n\nThis is the fact that reconciles `markovZ_bar_weight` (\"bar scales `z` by\n`q⁻⁴`\") with `QOU.MassTheory.barZ` (\"bar sends `z` to `z − h`\"): the two\nstatements are the same statement. Reading the weight as a *mere* rescaling —\none that leaves an `h` uncancelled — is what makes the strict average look\nbar-broken under D when it is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fNN_bar_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fNN_bar_weight","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L289-L306","doc":"Bar swap on the factors: the negative-crossing factor goes to\n`z/q⁴ + h` — **bar still exchanges the crossing chirality**, now against a\nweight-`−4` `z`.\n\n**This is the part of the C-era `fNN_bar` that survives.** That theorem read\n`f_nn(q⁻¹) = f_pp(q) + h(q)`, and its content was two independent facts: the\nsign flip on `h` (bar-odd — the skein swaps `σ ↔ σ⁻¹`) and the bar-invariance of\n`z`. Only the second is convention-dependent, so the chirality exchange — the\npart the name is about — is untouched; the `z` term carries `q⁻⁴`.\n\nConcretely: `heckeH_bar` is used verbatim, `markovZ_bar` is replaced by\n`markovZ_bar_weight`, and the `+ h` on the right-hand side is unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPP_bar_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPP_bar_weight","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L278-L287","doc":"Bar swap on the factors: the positive-crossing factor is bar-COVARIANT of\nweight `−4`, `f_pp(q⁻¹) = f_pp(q)/q⁴`.\n\n**Re-derived, not repaired (2026-08-26, bean `qou-cxjq`).** The convention-C\nstatement was `fPP s⁻¹ = fPP s` — bar-*invariance* — proved by one-line delegation\nto `markovZ_bar`. Since `f_pp = z` definitionally, this theorem is exactly as\nstrong as the bar behaviour of `z`, and inherits the weight that\n`markovZ_bar_weight` records. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.flavorDelta_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.flavorDelta_bar","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L268-L276","doc":"**`δ` bar behaviour**: `δ(q⁻¹) = −q²·δ(q)` (in `s`: `−s⁴·δ`). The flavor\nsplit is bar-odd up to the weight-two factor `q²` — consistent with its\n`ℏ_q²·h·[2]_q/3` decomposition (`ℏ_q(q⁻¹) = −q⁻¹·ℏ_q(q)` twice, `h` odd,\n`[2]_q` even). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.heckeH_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.heckeH_bar","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L261-L266","doc":"**`h` is bar-odd**: `h(q⁻¹) = −h(q)` — the Hecke skein parameter changes\nsign under the bar involution (the skein swaps `σ ↔ σ⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.markovZ_bar_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.markovZ_bar_weight","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L225-L259","doc":"**`z_D` is bar-COVARIANT of weight `−4`, not bar-even**:\n`z_D(q⁻¹) = z_D(q) / q⁴` (in `s`: divided by `s⁸`).\n\n**Replaces `markovZ_bar` (2026-08-26, bean `qou-cxjq`), which does not survive\nthe convention change.** That theorem asserted `z(q⁻¹) = z(q)` — *\"`z` is\nbar-even\"* — and it is a genuine property of convention C:\n`z_C(q⁻¹) = √(q⁻¹)/(q⁻¹+1) = √q/(q+1) = z_C(q)` identically. Convention D is\nneither bar-even nor bar-odd: `z_D(q⁻¹) = 1/(q³+q)` against `z_D(q) = q³/(q²+1)`,\nequal only at `q = 1`.\n\nSo this is a theorem that **does not survive**, not a proof that needed\nrepairing — the second such in this bean, after the bar-antisymmetry result in\n`nuclear-interactions/q-beta-cos-resummation.lean`, and the first stated as a\nnamed headline result.\n\n**What survives is better than nothing: the bar structure is graded rather than\ndestroyed.** The involution still acts on `z` cleanly, with weight `q⁻⁴` instead\nof trivially. Any downstream argument that used bar-evenness as a *symmetry* must\nnow carry that weight; an argument that only needed `z` to have *some* definite\nbar behaviour still has one.\n\nIndependently corroborated from the p-n side by `qou-1oxx` (\"the canonical p-n\nconvention is not bar-invariant\") and `QOU.QBeta.ZBarParity`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.inv_sq_add_one_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.inv_sq_add_one_eq","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L219-L223","doc":"Helper: `(s⁻¹)² + 1` is a unit multiple of `s² + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.markovZ_eq_sq_mul_inv_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.markovZ_eq_sq_mul_inv_sum","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L200-L217","doc":"**`z_D = q² · (q + q⁻¹)⁻¹`**: the defining form of the Markov parameter in\nconvention D, written in `s` with `q = s²`.\n\n**Replaces `markovZ_eq_inv_sqrt_sum` (2026-08-26, bean `qou-cxjq`).** That\ntheorem said `z = (s + s⁻¹)⁻¹`, i.e. `1/(√q + 1/√q)` — the convention-C defining\nidentity. It is **false** under convention D and was re-derived, not repaired:\n`(s + s⁻¹)⁻¹ = s/(s²+1) = √q/(q+1)`, which is convention C by definition.\n\nThe D form keeps the same `1/(x + x⁻¹)` shape but evaluates it at `x = q` rather\nthan `x = √q`, and rescales by `q²` — which is exactly the factorisation\n`z_D = q² · g(q)` of `QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD_eq_sq_mul_kernel`. The rescaling is\nnot cosmetic: no argument at all sends `g` to `z_D`, by\n`no_kernel_instantiation_is_conventionD`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPN","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L193-L196","doc":"Bring-color-weighted p-n interface factor\n`f_pn = z − h·(1/2 − δ/4)` (canonical convention since 2026-06-01,\n`closed_form_tau_M.closed_form_ratio` with the PROVEN leading `δ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fNN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fNN","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L189-L191","doc":"n-n interface factor `f_nn = z − h` (negative crossing, Markov axiom +\nHecke skein `σ⁻¹ = σ − h·1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.fPP","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L186-L187","doc":"p-p interface factor `f_pp = z` (positive crossing, Markov axiom). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.flavorDelta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.flavorDelta","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L179-L182","doc":"PROVEN leading flavor split `δ(q) = (q−1)²·(1−q⁻⁴)/3`\n(prop:flavor-split-substrate, `_li_2_q_util.flavor_split_leading`).\nIn `s`: `(s²−1)²·(1−s⁻⁸)/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.quantumTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.quantumTwo","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L176-L177","doc":"Quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` (in `s`: `s² + s⁻²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L173-L174","doc":"Substrate Planck parameter `ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹` (in `s`: `1 − s⁻²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.heckeH","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L170-L171","doc":"Hecke skein parameter `h = q − q⁻¹ = s² − s⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.markovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.ClosedForm.markovZ","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/ClosedFormInterfaceFactors.lean#L148-L168","doc":"Markov parameter in **convention D**, `z_D = q³/(q²+1)`, written in the\nsquare-root variable `s` (`q = s²`) as `s⁶/(s⁴+1)`.\n\n**Migrated from convention C 2026-08-26 (bean `qou-cxjq`).** This read\n`s/(s²+1)`, which at `q = s²` is `√q/(q+1)` — convention C. This file's\ndocstring is where the whole bean started: it states the `s`-substitution in\nplain English, and every detector missed it because the convention was hidden by\na change of variable rather than a change of form.\n\n**The `s` apparatus is now VESTIGIAL, and that is the follow-up this commit does\nnot do.** The entire reason for `s` was to express `√q` without `Real.sqrt`, so\nthe file could stay on the substrate side of the AGENTS.md §7c wall. Convention D\nhas no square root in it at all — `q³/(q²+1)` is rational in `q` directly — so\nthe substitution buys nothing here any more, and `s⁶/(s⁴+1)` is strictly uglier\nthan the `q` form it encodes. Rewriting the file in `q` is the right cleanup and\nis a separate, larger change across 22 theorems; doing it in the same commit as\nthe convention migration would make both unreviewable.\n\nMigrated in place because this module has **zero importers** — verified by module\nimport, not by name grep — so no recorded statement outside it changes meaning. ","signatureChunk":0}]}